-- =============================================================================
-- University of Nigeria, Nsukka — Faculty of Engineering
-- "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" block (CHE 302 – CHE 517)
-- =============================================================================
-- WHY THIS IS NOT A "Chemical Engineering" DEPARTMENT OUTLINE
--
-- The Faculty of Engineering handbook prints a block of sixteen CHE-coded
-- courses under the heading "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" (book pages
-- 167-170). It does NOT print a Chemical Engineering programme structure:
-- there is no Chemical Engineering chapter, no year-by-year timetable, and no
-- entry for it in the handbook's department chapters. The CHE block sits
-- inside the Mechanical Engineering chapter — every one of those pages carries
-- the running footer "Department of Mechanical Engineering" — immediately
-- after ME 591 (Engineering Metallurgy) and immediately before a "SERVICE
-- COURSES" block.
--
-- That was checked against UNN's own website before deciding how to file it:
--   * The official Faculty of Engineering site (engineering.unn.edu.ng) lists
--     its departments as Agric & Bioresources, Biomedical, Civil, Electrical,
--     Electronic & Computer, Mechanical, Metallurgical & Materials,
--     Mechatronic, and Automotive Engineering. Chemical Engineering is not
--     among them.
--   * UNN's Chemical Engineering department was closed and has not been
--     reinstated, which is consistent with the handbook printing CHE course
--     descriptions without any accompanying degree programme.
--
-- So these rows are filed under Mechanical Engineering — the department whose
-- chapter actually prints them — and flagged is_elective = true. Creating a
-- "Chemical Engineering" department in this app would invent a programme that
-- UNN does not currently run, and would show up in the department picker as a
-- degree a student could enrol in.
--
-- LEVEL: taken from the course code's own hundreds digit (CHE 3xx -> 300
-- Level, 4xx -> 400 Level, 5xx -> 500 Level), which is the numbering
-- convention this handbook uses throughout.
--
-- SEMESTER — READ THIS: unlike every other course in this app's outline data,
-- these sixteen carry NO stated semester. They appear only in the handbook's
-- course-description section, never in a programme-structure table, so the
-- handbook never says which semester they run in. They are stored with
-- semester = 'first' purely because the column is NOT NULL and 'first' is its
-- default — that value is a placeholder, NOT a claim from the source. Each
-- row's description says so explicitly so a student is never misled.
--
-- CREDIT UNITS: taken from the "(N units)" marker printed at the end of each
-- description. CHE 302's marker is right-aligned onto the following heading
-- line by the handbook's own layout; it reads 2 units.
-- =============================================================================

delete from public.course_outlines
 where institution = 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka'
   and department = 'Mechanical Engineering'
   and course_code like 'CHE %';

insert into public.course_outlines
  (course_code, course_title, institution, faculty, department, level,
   semester, credit_units, description, topics, contributor_name, is_elective)
values
  ('CHE 302', 'Industrial Process Calculation', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Material and Energy Balancing of Physical and Chemical Systems for steady state and transient conditions. Introduction to Analysis and Synthesis of chemical processes. Unit and Dimensions. Stoichiometric and composition relations principles of material balances: Process involving chemical reactions: Stepwise counter current Processing; Inventory change in multi-effect evaporations. Triangular diagrams. Energy Balance: The Use of Thermodynamic diagrams, Thermochemical data, Steam tables, etc. in the calculation of heat effects in industrial plants. Combined material and energy balances. Unsteady-state material and energy balances. A wide range of industrial chemical, metallurgical and petroleum processes is used for illustration.', '["Material and Energy Balancing of Physical and Chemical Systems for steady state and transient conditions", "Introduction to Analysis and Synthesis of chemical processes. Unit and Dimensions", "Stoichiometric and composition relations principles of material balances; process involving chemical reactions; stepwise counter current processing", "Energy Balance: use of thermodynamic diagrams, thermochemical data and steam tables in the calculation of heat effects in industrial plants", "Combined material and energy balances. Unsteady-state material and energy balances"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 401', 'Heat and Mass Transfer', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. HEAT TRANSFER: Nature of Processes of conduction, convection and radiation. Definition of Thermal conductivity and heat transfer by convection. Heat exchangers, Radiation. Heat Transfer to boiling condensation of vapors. Heat Transfer to boiling liquids. MASS TRANSFER: Simultaneous Heat and Mass Transfer. Humidification of gases. Drying types of driers. Evaporation. Heat Transfer Coefficients in evaporators. Distillation batch and continuous distillation and fractionation. Plate Columns-efficiency; pressure drop and stability. TRANSPORT PHENOMENA: Basic derivation of transport properties based on kinetic theory of gases. Basic laws of momentum and energy transport analogies. Measurement and calculations of transport coefficients.', '["HEAT TRANSFER: nature of processes of conduction, convection and radiation; thermal conductivity; heat exchangers; radiation", "Heat transfer to boiling condensation of vapors and to boiling liquids", "MASS TRANSFER: simultaneous heat and mass transfer; humidification of gases; drying types of driers", "Evaporation; heat transfer coefficients in evaporators; batch and continuous distillation and fractionation; plate columns", "TRANSPORT PHENOMENA: transport properties from kinetic theory of gases; momentum and energy transport analogies; measurement and calculation of transport coefficients"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 402', 'Chemical Engineering Process Design', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 4, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. A design problem involving the study of a chemical process or part of such process, including drawing up a flowsheet, the preparation of heat and mass balances and detailed design of some plant items. Presentation and discussion of real process design problems. Block diagrams, process and engineering flow diagrams, process out line chart incorporating methods study, critical examination. Specification of vessels, examples include distillation towers and ancillaries, heat exchangers vaporizers knockout vessels. Emphasis on conception and invention of processes as well as analysis and economic balance, to specify optimum and operation conditions. Discussion of a variety of cases.', '["A design problem involving the study of a chemical process or part of such process", "Drawing up a flowsheet, preparation of heat and mass balances, detailed design of plant items", "Block diagrams, process and engineering flow diagrams, process outline chart incorporating methods study and critical examination", "Specification of vessels: distillation towers and ancillaries, heat exchangers, vaporizers, knockout vessels", "Conception and invention of processes; analysis and economic balance to specify optimum operating conditions"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 403', 'Separation Processes', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Principles of Separating Homogeneous Mixtures. Design of staged separation processes including distillations, absorption, and extraction. Physical properties of importance to separation processes. Leaching and extraction with immiscible solvents. Binary distillation. Continuous contact columns. Application to isothermal gas absorption. Packed and plate columns hydrodynamic limitation and performance data. General diffusion equation and penetration theory. Mass transfer with chemical reaction. Solvent extraction. Distillation of multi component mixtures. Computational procedure for rectification columns. Extractive and azeotropic distillation. Multi-component absorption design procedures. Crystallization.', '["Principles of separating homogeneous mixtures; design of staged separation processes including distillation, absorption and extraction", "Leaching and extraction with immiscible solvents; binary distillation", "Continuous contact columns; application to isothermal gas absorption; packed and plate columns", "General diffusion equation and penetration theory; mass transfer with chemical reaction", "Solvent extraction; distillation of multi-component mixtures; extractive and azeotropic distillation; crystallization"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 404', 'Particle Fluid Mechanics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Particle Fluid Mechanics: Motion of single particles and crios in a fluid. Types of centrifuges; sedimentation law of single fluids through packed beds. Counter-current and co-current flow of fluids through packed columns. Filtration-constant-rate sand constant pressure filtration. Selection of equipment. Fluidization; heat and mass transfer, and chemical reaction in fluidized beds. Peneumatic and hydraulic conveyance. Particle size reduction and distributions; equipment. Mixing fluids and solids.', '["Motion of single particles in a fluid; types of centrifuges; sedimentation", "Counter-current and co-current flow of fluids through packed columns", "Filtration: constant-rate and constant-pressure filtration; selection of equipment", "Fluidization; heat and mass transfer and chemical reaction in fluidized beds", "Pneumatic and hydraulic conveyance; particle size reduction and distributions; mixing fluids and solids"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 405', 'Reaction Kinetics and Design', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Application of descriptive kinetics to the interpretation of rate and selectivity data in homogeneous reactions. Development of reaction rate equations from the theory of chemical kinetics. Development and analysis of idealized reactor models with applications of design and deviations from ideality. Introduction to the theory of diffusion and reaction in two-phase systems. Detailed study of the theory of chemical kinetics. Collision theory and its extensions. Transition state theory of surface-catalyzed reactions. Analysis of reaction mechanisms and the role of mechanistic studies in chemical reaction engineering.', '["Application of descriptive kinetics to the interpretation of rate and selectivity data in homogeneous reactions", "Development of reaction rate equations from the theory of chemical kinetics", "Development and analysis of idealized reactor models; deviations from ideality", "Theory of diffusion and reaction in two-phase systems", "Collision theory and its extensions; transition state theory of surface-catalyzed reactions; analysis of reaction mechanisms"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 406', 'Chemical Reaction Engineering', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Review of fundamentals of chemical thermodynamics of chemical kinetics, as would be relevant to reactor design homogeneous reactions. Heterogeneous reactions. Tabular reactors continuous stirred-tank reactors. Fluidized and choice of reactors. Optimization. Conditions of stability of reactors. Scale-up procedure-batch and continuous flow reactors. Economic evaluation and comparison of reactor types.', '["Review of fundamentals of chemical thermodynamics and chemical kinetics relevant to reactor design", "Homogeneous and heterogeneous reactions", "Tubular reactors and continuous stirred-tank reactors; fluidized reactors and choice of reactors", "Optimization and conditions of stability of reactors", "Scale-up procedure for batch and continuous flow reactors; economic evaluation and comparison of reactor types"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 407', 'Chemical Engineering Laboratory', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '400 Level', 'first', 2, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Experiments in physical measurements. Fluid mechanics. Heat transfer and refrigeration. Emphasis on investigation of basic relationships important in engineering. Experimental design, analysis of results, and preparation of engineering reports are stressed. Experiments in mass transfer simultaneous heat and mass transfer, vaporization and condensation, and separation techniques.', '["Experiments in physical measurements", "Fluid mechanics; heat transfer and refrigeration", "Investigation of basic relationships important in engineering", "Experimental design, analysis of results and preparation of engineering reports", "Experiments in mass transfer, simultaneous heat and mass transfer, vaporization and condensation, and separation techniques"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 502', 'Process Dynamics and Control', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. The development of mathematical models to describe the transient response characteristics of basic process elements; linearization techniques and the development of linear transfer functions; closed-loop analysis from the view of stability and transient response. The analysis of feedback and feed-forward control systems. The design of compensating networks from frequency response data.', '["Development of mathematical models to describe the transient response characteristics of basic process elements", "Linearization techniques and the development of linear transfer functions", "Closed-loop analysis from the view of stability and transient response", "Analysis of feedback and feed-forward control systems", "Design of compensating networks from frequency response data"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 503', 'Process Design and Optimization', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. General approach to the design of chemical processing units and plants; cost estimates and chemical process economics; optimization techniques; linear programming. Modern techniques of optimization and their application to the design and operation of chemical systems. Consideration of both steady state and dynamic methods with emphasis on procedures involving experimental search for the optimum. Optimal design and operation of large-scale chemical processing systems; mathematical methods; process modeling; directed search for optimum conditions. Linear and dynamic programming solutions.', '["General approach to the design of chemical processing units and plants", "Cost estimates and chemical process economics", "Optimization techniques; linear programming; modern techniques of optimization applied to the design and operation of chemical systems", "Steady state and dynamic methods; experimental search for the optimum", "Optimal design and operation of large-scale chemical processing systems; process modeling; linear and dynamic programming solutions"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 505', 'Chemical Plant Design', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. An introduction to process engineering and project engineering and management. Critical path methods; project Evaluation and Review Technique; Consideration in process unit synthesis and selection; plant location and Consideration; process and mechanical flow diagrams; materials of fabrication and selection; design and selection of piping, valves and pressure vessels, pumps, compressors and control systems. Detailed design of large-scale commercial plants involving the specification of chemical processing equipment such as heaters, heat exchangers, contacting and separating equipment. Other topics covered include: operational considerations in design; plant safety relief system design; waste treatment and pollution control processes; design and selection of off site facilities.', '["Introduction to process engineering and project engineering and management", "Critical path methods; Project Evaluation and Review Technique; consideration in process unit synthesis and selection", "Plant location; process and mechanical flow diagrams; materials of fabrication and selection", "Design and selection of piping, valves and pressure vessels, pumps, compressors and control systems", "Detailed design of large-scale commercial plants; plant safety relief system design; waste treatment and pollution control processes"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 506', 'Industrial Chemical Technology', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Review of the manufacturing processes of various heavy chemicals and intermediates these include suphuric, Hydrochloric, and Nitric acids, Ammonia, Caustic Soda, soaps and Detergents, Petrochemicals. Fuel and Industrial Gases Electrochemical, Fertilizers Cement, Pulp and Paper Industrial Fermentation Processes. Metal Ore processing. Nuclear Materials, and Sugar. These are to be considered withy regard to: availability of raw materials and economics methods of production. Kinetics of processes: necessary operating conditions; selection of catalyst; appropriate choice and design of a reactor; integration of the reactor with the rest of the commercial unit; pant location, etc.', '["Review of the manufacturing processes of various heavy chemicals and intermediates: sulphuric, hydrochloric and nitric acids, ammonia, caustic soda, soaps and detergents", "Petrochemicals; fuel and industrial gases; electrochemicals; fertilizers; cement", "Pulp and paper; industrial fermentation processes; metal ore processing; nuclear materials; sugar", "Availability of raw materials and economic methods of production", "Kinetics of processes: operating conditions, selection of catalyst, choice and design of a reactor, integration with the rest of the commercial unit, plant location"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 511', 'Environmental Engineering', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Pollution and the environment - definitions and inter-relationship, natural and man-made pollution, the economics of pollution. Air pollution gaseous and particulate pollutants and their sources. Effects on weather, vegetation, materials, and human health. Legislation relating to air pollution. Methods of control of gaseous and particulate pollutant: absorption, adsorption, combustion, catalytic destruction, cyclones, inertia separators, electrostatic precipitators, bag filters, wet washer, etc. Dispersal form chimneys and methods of calculating chimney height. Flare stacks. Water Pollution - River pollution by industrial effluents. Legislation and standards for effluent discharge. Impurities in natural waters and their effects. Brief survey of river ecology and the effects of effluents on the ecosystems. Treatment processes including precipitation, flocculation, coagulation, sedimentation. Clarification and colour removal. Principles of biological treatment processes. Cost of treatment of water refuse on exchange, cooling water treatment. Land Pollution: Disposal of solid wastes by in conversion of solid wastes into useful materials or energy. Treatment of other types of pollution - Noise: Thermal and Nuclear pollution.', '["Pollution and the environment: definitions and inter-relationship, natural and man-made pollution, the economics of pollution", "Air pollution: gaseous and particulate pollutants and their sources; effects on weather, vegetation, materials and human health; legislation", "Methods of control of gaseous and particulate pollutants: absorption, adsorption, combustion, catalytic destruction, cyclones, electrostatic precipitators, bag filters", "Water pollution: river pollution by industrial effluents; treatment processes including precipitation, flocculation, coagulation, sedimentation; biological treatment", "Land pollution: disposal and conversion of solid wastes; noise, thermal and nuclear pollution"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 512', 'Biochemical Engineering', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Introduction to Biochemistry, Enzyme Kinetics. Thermodynamics of aqueous reactions, industrial microbiological processes, photosynthesis, and separation processes for biological materials; Design and control of fermentation equipment. Isolation and development of microbes for hydrocarbon conversions. Background for both biomedical engineering and biochemical engineering.', '["Introduction to biochemistry; enzyme kinetics", "Thermodynamics of aqueous reactions; industrial microbiological processes; photosynthesis", "Separation processes for biological materials", "Design and control of fermentation equipment", "Isolation and development of microbes for hydrocarbon conversions"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 513', 'Pulp and Paper Technology', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Cellulose and Hemicellulose-structures and characteristic Lignia. Pulp wood-types and properties. Types of pulping processes-sulphite, alkalia mechanical, deminmechanical, etc. Bleaching Power preparation, nature of fibre bending. Sheet formation. Water Usage and disposal in pulp and power industries. Microbiology. Internal and surfacing waste strength. Colouring. Properties of paper, pigment paper and paper plastics.', '["Cellulose and hemicellulose structures; lignin; pulp wood types and properties", "Types of pulping processes: sulphite, alkaline, mechanical, semi-mechanical", "Bleaching power preparation; nature of fibre bonding; sheet formation", "Water usage and disposal in pulp and paper industries; microbiology", "Properties of paper, pigment paper and paper plastics"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 516', 'Chemical Engineering Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Mathematical techniques for handling rate problems such as diffusion, heat transfer, and chemical reactions, classical theory of minima and maxima-function, equality constraints. Language multipliers. Linear programming methods and applications. Non-linear programming and numerical optimization techniques for steady state problems. Dynamic programming, application to stage wise chemical engineering processes. Ponttryagin''s Maximum Principle, application to optimal design of chemical reactors. Algorithms for optimizing dynamic systems, boundary iteration, control interaction, first order and conjugate gradient methods in function space, second order techniques.', '["Mathematical techniques for handling rate problems such as diffusion, heat transfer and chemical reactions", "Classical theory of minima and maxima; equality constraints; Lagrange multipliers", "Linear programming methods and applications; non-linear programming and numerical optimization for steady state problems", "Dynamic programming applied to stagewise chemical engineering processes; Pontryagin''s Maximum Principle applied to optimal design of chemical reactors", "Algorithms for optimizing dynamic systems: boundary iteration, control interaction, first order and conjugate gradient methods, second order techniques"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true),
  ('CHE 517', 'Coal and Coke Technology', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Mechanical Engineering', '500 Level', 'first', 3, 'Printed in the handbook under "CHEMICAL ENGINEERING COURSES" within the Mechanical Engineering chapter; the handbook states no semester for this course. Origin of Coal-effect of different degrees of coalification and geological age on rock, composition and petrographic constituents of coal. Different coal types. Sampling and Analysis of coal. Standard tests and their significance. Determination of the coking properties of coals. Coal classification. The coking mechanism. Significance of the plastic layer and condition of carbonization. Production and properties of coke for different uses - monitoring tests and their significance. Preparation and cleaning of coal. Float and sink tests. Different lasting processes and plants in the treatment of gas and recovery of by-products from the carbonization process.', '["Origin of coal; effect of degrees of coalification and geological age on composition and petrographic constituents", "Different coal types; sampling and analysis of coal; standard tests and their significance", "Determination of the coking properties of coals; coal classification", "The coking mechanism; significance of the plastic layer and condition of carbonization; production and properties of coke", "Preparation and cleaning of coal; float and sink tests; treatment of gas and recovery of by-products from the carbonization process"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', true);
